{
  "_meta": {
    "name": "customer-registration-and-storefront-checkout",
    "description": "One owner sets up a company, two branches, and products; a separate shopper registers as a customer and checks out.",
    "journey": [
      "Owner registers an account in Firebase Authentication.",
      "Owner creates a company.",
      "Owner creates branch documents linked to their stores by storeId.",
      "Owner creates active products for the main branch.",
      "A visitor browses the main branch and adds products to a cart; browsing itself creates no Firestore document.",
      "Visitor registers a separate account; the new account receives the customer permission.",
      "The registered customer completes checkout and the order links to that customer's UID."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Create the owner Firebase Authentication account in the app first. Firestore fixtures cannot create Auth accounts or passwords.",
      "Replace the owner UID and email placeholders with the values from the account created in the app.",
      "The storefront reads canonical stores, branches, and products through the integrations API; the API exposes only browse-safe product fields.",
      "The shopper in this fixture is a sample-only profile and cannot sign in; use a real shopper UID/email if you want a sign-in-capable customer.",
      "Public storefront documents contain only browse-safe fields; internal store and product documents remain private.",
      "To browse this sample company, open /branches?companyId=sample-company-001.",
      "Checkout requires a signed-in customer and links the order to that customer's UID."
    ]
  },
